IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- THE INSTRUMENTS AFTER ACT 15 OF 2017 THAT AMEND THE TELECOMMUNICATIONS ACT 1999 (deposited 2026-11-04 from the e-Gazette's two follow-up lists; each file is TA1999.<NAME>.txt under registers/source-bundle/).
-- Eight Acts and one Order: Act 26 of 2018 (s 61), Act 15 of 2019 (s 187), Act 40 of 2018 (s 517), Act 4 of 2021 (s 22(9)), Act 25 of 2021 (s 212), Act 12 of 2020 (s 50(4)(g)), Act 13 of 2026 (s 18), Act 31 of 2022 (s 21(7)) and G.N. No. S 26/2022 (paragraph 22).
-- They are all the instruments the Legislative History of the 2026 consolidation lists after Act 15 of 2017 (TA1999.txt:7192-7302).  The type is named "Instrument" because S 26/2022 is an Order, not an Act.
-- Seven commence by Ministerial appointment or on a day the Legislative History names; their commencement notifications are NOT deposited.  So, as for Act 15 of 2017 in sgta-ta-versions.l4, the EFFECTIVE day is the Legislative History's ("Commencement" line, quoted below)
-- and the day a reader could see that date is ASSUMED to be the same day.  For TWO the published day is read: Act 31 of 2022, whose commencement notification S 850/2022 was first published on 31 October 2022 and brings the Act (with exceptions that do not include s 21) into operation
-- on 1 November 2022; and S 26/2022, which carries its own commencement (paragraph 1(1): 13 January 2022, except paragraph 12) and was first published on 12 January 2022 at 7 pm.  The day each Act was first published is the Gazette's "First published" line (also quoted).
--
-- WHAT EACH CHANGES (the TA's own numbering as the instrument prints it; Acts 26/2018, 15/2019, 40/2018, 4/2021, 25/2021 and 12/2020 use the 2000 Edition numbers, Act 13/2026, Act 31/2022 and S 26/2022 the 2020 Edition numbers):
--   Act 26 of 2018   s 58: inserts subsection (10) (no direction under s 58 while an activation order under the Public Order and Safety (Special Powers) Act 2018 is in force, for the purposes of a direction under section 32 of that Act).
--   Act 15 of 2019   repeals s 45 (sending false message) and deletes "45," in s 60(3).
--   Act 40 of 2018   ss 32I(3)(b), 32J(3)(a), (b), (c) and (6), 32L(1)(b), (c) and (2)(a), (b), (c): references to the Companies Act replaced by references to the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018; new s 32J(3)(ba), s 32L(1)(ca) and s 32L(2)(ba).
--   Act 4 of 2021    s 2, definition of "owner": removes the HUDC housing estate words from paragraph (b) and sub-paragraph (b)(iv).
--   Act 25 of 2021   s 25(1) ("in execution" -> "under or pursuant to an enforcement order"); ss 29(8), 33(7), 47(5), 49(5) ("leave" -> "permission"); s 32L(1)(e) (delete "execute or").
--   Act 12 of 2020   s 2, definitions of "common property" and of "owner" (paragraph (a)(iii)): "Building Maintenance and Strata Management Act" -> "Building (Strata Management) Act".
--   Act 31 of 2022   s 46(3)(b): "Part 7" -> "Parts 7 and 9" (of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018).
--   S 26/2022        s 2: "(including a VCC)" after "to a company" in "securities", and new definitions "VCC" and "VCC Act"; ss 40(7)(a) and 41(7)(a): "and the Trustees Act 1967" -> ", the Trustees Act 1967 and the VCC Act".
--   Act 13 of 2026   ss 37(13), 37(14), 38(9) to (13), 40(11), 42(1), 92(3)(c)(iv), 92(6), 92(12), 92(19), 92(20) and 97(2)(ga) (2020 Edition numbers).
-- WHAT IS ON THE DECISIVE CHAIN.  The provisions of the Act that the receiver question turns on are s 2 "equipment", "radio-communication" and "broadcasting apparatus", s 5, ss 33 to 36 (2020: 53 to 56), s 65 (2020: 85), s 72 (2020: 95) and s 73 (2020: 96).
--   Only ONE amended provision is on that chain: Act 25 of 2021 changes "leave" to "permission" in s 33(7), now s 53(7), the notice-of-defence subsection of the licensing offence (quoted below with the 2000 Edition's words and the consolidation's).  It changes no condition of the offence.
--   Acts 4 of 2021 and 12 of 2020 amend s 2, but the definitions "owner" and "common property", not the three that the chain uses.
-- THE SEAT (sgta-tv-*.l4) does not consult this module: its version table still has the one row "as amended by Acts after Act 15 of 2017 that are not deposited" (sgta-ta-versions.l4), so nothing here changes an answer.
--   NOTES.md says what wiring these Acts into that table would change.

DECLARE `Instrument amending the Telecommunications Act after Act 15 of 2017` IS ONE OF
    `Act 26 of 2018`
    `Act 15 of 2019`
    `Act 40 of 2018`
    `Act 4 of 2021`
    `Act 25 of 2021`
    `Act 12 of 2020`
    `Act 13 of 2026`
    `Act 31 of 2022`
    `G.N. No. S 26/2022`

